  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) The paper aims to investigate how a bubble trapped beneath the upper wall of a vertically vibrated liquid chamber can undergo resonant coupling between the imposed oscillation and bubble shape modes, producing spontaneous symmetry breaking and tunable galloping motions, including rectilinear, orbital, and run-and-tumble motion, as an inertia-based mechanism for steering and applying bubbles in nearly inviscid flows.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) Complex, useful, and controllable bubble dynamics motivate studying vibration-driven galloping as a mechanism for directing bubble motion."];
